-- title:
--   Separability of Frobenius-fixed elements over 𝔽_{p^r}(t)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field and $F$ a field extension of $K$ (as a $K$-algebra), let $p$ be a prime and $r$ a positive natural number, and suppose $F$ has characteristic $p$. Let $\varphi \colon F \to F$ be a $K$-algebra endomorphism, and let $t \in F$ be transcendental over $K$ with $\varphi(t) = t^{p^r}$. Assume that $F$ is separable as an algebra over the intermediate field $K(t) =$ `IntermediateField.adjoin K {t}`, i.e. every element of $F$ is separable over $K(t)$. Then for every $g \in F$ satisfying $\varphi(g) = g^{p^r}$, the element $g$ is separable over the subfield of $F$ generated by the union of the set $\{c \in F : c^{p^r} = c\}$ of roots of $X^{p^r} - X$ in $F$ with $\{t\}$; that is, $g$ is algebraic over that subfield and its minimal polynomial there is separable. The generating set $\{c : c^{p^r} = c\}$ is the fixed field of the $p^r$-power map on $F$, a copy of $F \cap \mathbb{F}_{p^r}$, so the conclusion says that $g$ is separable algebraic over $\mathbb{F}_{p^r}(t)$.
--
--   This is the descent statement that the elements of $F$ on which a $K$-linear endomorphism acting on the coordinate $t$ by $t \mapsto t^{p^r}$ agrees with the absolute $p^r$-power map are separable algebraic over $\mathbb{F}_{p^r}(t)$, with no hypothesis that $K$ be algebraic over $\mathbb{F}_p$. It is used in the construction of a curve over a finite field together with an isomorphism realising a given power map, via [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_isCurveOver_adjoin_range_eq_top_apply_algEquiv_eq_pow_of_pow_eq_one`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_isCurveOver_adjoin_range_eq_top_apply_algEquiv_eq_pow_of_pow_eq_one).
